WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.733
Inheritance.

2
00:00:02.033 --> 00:00:06.367
A subclass can reuse a parent's code and change only the parts that differ.

3
00:00:07.567 --> 00:00:11.267
A subclass inherits every attribute and method from its parent.

4
00:00:11.567 --> 00:00:13.833
It can override the ones it wants to change.

5
00:00:14.133 --> 00:00:18.367
And it reaches the parent's version through super, most often in the constructor.

6
00:00:19.567 --> 00:00:20.867
Here's the family tree.

7
00:00:21.167 --> 00:00:24.367
Everything in Python ultimately descends from object.

8
00:00:24.667 --> 00:00:26.767
SpaceProbe is the general parent.

9
00:00:27.067 --> 00:00:32.600
Lander and Orbiter are specialized children that reuse what works and override what differs.

10
00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:37.567
When you call a method, Python walks a lookup order called the MRO.

11
00:00:37.867 --> 00:00:40.167
It checks the instance's own class first.

12
00:00:40.467 --> 00:00:41.433
Then the parent.

13
00:00:41.733 --> 00:00:43.009
And finally object.

14
00:00:43.009 --> 00:00:46.367
The first match wins, which is why overrides work.

15
00:00:47.567 --> 00:00:49.067
Here's the pattern in code.

16
00:00:49.367 --> 00:00:52.833
Lander lists SpaceProbe in parentheses, so it inherits from it.

17
00:00:53.133 --> 00:00:56.833
Its constructor calls super, so the parent still sets up the name.

18
00:00:57.133 --> 00:00:59.900
Then it overrides describe with its own version.

19
00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:03.567
Here's inheritance in a retrieval system.

20
00:01:03.867 --> 00:01:06.867
A base retriever class defines a retrieve method.

21
00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:11.600
The vector and keyword retrievers subclass it, overriding only the search.

22
00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:15.070
So one evaluation harness can score any retriever.

23
00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:17.733
LangChain's source is built like this too.

24
00:01:18.933 --> 00:01:20.967
The common mistake is going too deep.

25
00:01:21.267 --> 00:01:26.000
Keep hierarchies shallow, and prefer composition when you're tempted to add more levels.

26
00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:28.041
Let's recap.

27
00:01:28.041 --> 00:01:30.633
Subclasses reuse and extend a parent.

28
00:01:30.933 --> 00:01:34.100
Override what differs, and call super to cooperate.

29
00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:37.067
Python finds methods in MRO order.

30
00:01:37.367 --> 00:01:38.489
Keep it shallow.

31
00:01:38.489 --> 00:01:40.033
Next up: polymorphism.
